# Acts and roles

Room state derives from ⟦f:principal-keys⟧three ⟦/f⟧kinds of act only. Seats that are members with no
add, and the seat ingest starts, stand beside them (Seat). Each act belongs to
exactly one kind (LANE-31).

- **Room act**: An act signed by a seat key, wherever it is taken. It is checked
  against the capabilities of the seat's role and the room state; create room⟦f:work-rooms⟧,
  join, a join request and leave⟦/f⟧ are checked against ⟦f:shared-rooms⟧admission and ⟦/f⟧the add
  instead. The room acts are create room⟦f:work-rooms⟧, join, a join request, leave, a role
  request⟦/f⟧⟦f:conversation⟧, post⟦/f⟧, link, pin, edit, unpin⟦f:moderation⟧, list removal⟦/f⟧⟦f:presentations⟧, present, pick⟦/f⟧⟦f:moderation⟧, kick⟦/f⟧⟦f:shared-rooms⟧, bar,
  unbar⟦/f⟧⟦f:moderation⟧, mute and unmute⟦/f⟧⟦f:work-rooms⟧; set title, labels or an assignment⟦/f⟧⟦f:facilitator⟧; and write a room
  summary or a summary request⟦/f⟧.⟦f:work-rooms⟧ A leave⟦f:moderation⟧, kick⟦/f⟧⟦f:shared-rooms⟧ or bar⟦/f⟧ never drops a room's
  qualifying pins from a run's restore block, within the foreign-room limit of
  Relations.⟦/f⟧ A pin, edit or unpin room act never changes any restore block: an
  author's own pin, edit and unpin act only on pins that do not restore⟦f:stamps⟧
  unstamped⟦/f⟧⟦f:moderation⟧, and a list removal only takes a pin off the pin list⟦/f⟧. A link act
  adds one range link⟦f:work-rooms⟧⟦f:git-tracking⟧, branch link⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧⟦f:intent-criteria⟧ or criterion link⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧. Create room is the first
  act of the creating seat's writer. Room acts are governance, not I2 trust: on
  their own they never widen what reaches an agent, which only principal acts⟦f:stamps⟧
  such as ⟦f:trust-grants⟧a trust grant, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:endorsement⟧an endorsement or ⟦/f⟧a stamp⟦/f⟧ do, and OWN-11's classes do
  not cover them.
- **Principal act**: An act of a kind OWN-11 classes, taken at a principal
  surface. It is ⟦f:principal-keys⟧signed by a device key once PRV-10 ships; before then it is ⟦/f⟧an
  `operator` event its device seat's seal covers, told apart from a room act by
  the principal surface it is marked with (OWN-02). An act a seat key signs as
  the act, beyond sealing its writer, is a room act. A widening act lets more
  reach an agent, or more act or leave the node; a cut act only stops, narrows
  or undoes a widening; a neutral act does neither, such as acknowledging
  counters. ⟦f:work-rooms⟧Every change of visibility⟦f:shared-rooms⟧, admission⟦/f⟧⟦f:moderation⟧ or a room setting⟦/f⟧ is widening,
  whichever way it goes. ⟦/f⟧Its classes:
  - **Cut:** ⟦f:held-requests⟧deny, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:launcher⟧interrupt, pause or stop a run, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:delegation-grants⟧cancel a delegation, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:held-requests⟧end a
    permission grant, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:bundle-import⟧reject a foreign room, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:work-rooms⟧decline a join request, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:rule-levels⟧tighten a
    rule level, ⟦/f⟧revoke a role assignment, ⟦f:ci-attestation⟧revoke a CI key, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:publishing⟧stop publishing a
    room, ⟦/f⟧quarantine content without removing anything from a restore block,
    ⟦f:sandbox-risk⟧withdraw a risk acceptance, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:trust-grants⟧revoke a trust grant, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:delegation-grants⟧end a delegation grant⟦f:acceptance-grants⟧ or
    an acceptance grant⟦/f⟧, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:away-policy⟧turn an away policy off, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:ownership-transfer⟧withdraw a named successor,
    ⟦/f⟧⟦f:moderation⟧revoke an appointment, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:stamps⟧unstamp a pin version, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:notices⟧turn notices off, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:ownership-transfer⟧decline a
    handover, withdraw as successor, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:endorsement⟧⟦f:conversation⟧dismiss a directed post, ⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:key-revocation⟧revoke ⟦f:access-tokens⟧an access
    token, ⟦/f⟧a seat key⟦f:service-accounts⟧ or a service account's certificate⟦/f⟧, ⟦/f⟧turn capture on⟦f:launcher⟧, and
    turn off ⟦f:browser-room-view⟧the room-view component, ⟦/f⟧the launcher⟦f:peer-sync⟧, the peer component⟦/f⟧⟦f:git-carrier⟧, the
    publish component⟦/f⟧⟦f:bridges⟧, a bridge⟦/f⟧⟦f:git-carrier⟧ or the git carrier⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧.
  - **Neutral:** ⟦f:room-status⟧mark a room ready, its **ready mark** (the owner⟦f:moderation⟧⟦f:shared-rooms⟧ or a principal
    whose device seat in the room is a moderator⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧), or abandoned, its **abandoned
    mark** (the owner), acknowledge an overlap, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧record a `met`, `not met` or
    `needs changes` verdict, unpin a verdict, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:room-view-surfaces⟧open the forensic view, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:purge-retention⟧⟦f:shared-rooms⟧make a
    purge request, ⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:peer-sync⟧refuse a quarantine request⟦f:purge-retention⟧, an erasure request⟦/f⟧⟦f:purge-retention⟧⟦f:shared-rooms⟧ or a purge
    request⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧⟦f:git-tracking⟧choose a branch to compare, ⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧acknowledge counters, ⟦f:needs-you⟧dismiss a Q3 or
    Q4 item⟦f:endorsement⟧⟦f:conversation⟧ other than a directed post⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧, ⟦/f⟧unpin a pin its own agent's run seat
    wrote⟦f:needs-you⟧, and add a room to or remove it from the focus set⟦/f⟧.
  - **Widening:** ⟦f:held-requests⟧allow, answer a hand-off (a hand-back), reply, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:launcher⟧steer, confirm
    a steer for a later turn (OWN-13), ⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧⟦f:git-tracking⟧send a correction, retry from a worktree
    checkpoint, ⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:intent-criteria⟧set or revise an intent, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:launcher⟧resume, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:delegation-grants⟧record a delegation grant⟦f:acceptance-grants⟧ or an
    acceptance grant⟦/f⟧, ⟦/f⟧add, edit or unpin a pin of a type that restores written
    from a device seat a device key certified (⟦f:principal-keys⟧before PRV-10 ships, ⟦/f⟧this node's
    own device seat), ⟦f:pin-candidates⟧confirm a pin candidate, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:work-rooms⟧change a room's visibility,
    ⟦/f⟧⟦f:shared-rooms⟧⟦f:principal-keys⟧invite a principal key, ⟦f:access-tokens⟧issue an invite link, ⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:segment-exchange⟧choose a fork, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:launcher⟧turn on ⟦f:browser-room-view⟧the
    room-view component or ⟦/f⟧the launcher by accepting the configuration that
    turns it on (ADM-04), ⟦/f⟧⟦f:peer-sync⟧turn on the peer⟦f:git-carrier⟧ or publish⟦/f⟧ component, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:browser-room-view⟧issue a
    phone-scoped room-view secret, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:ownership-transfer⟧accept a handover or succession, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:work-rooms⟧ask for a
    device seat's join to a room its principal has no member seat in, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:work-rooms⟧ask for or
    accept a join⟦f:shared-rooms⟧, which sends the run's events to a room other principals'
    nodes hold⟦/f⟧, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:endorsement⟧endorse, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:rule-levels⟧loosen a rule level, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:away-policy⟧turn on or change an away policy
    other than turning it off, ⟦/f⟧quarantine that removes a pin⟦f:landmarks⟧ or a landmark⟦/f⟧ from
    a restore block, release a quarantine, ⟦f:purge-retention⟧purge⟦f:peer-sync⟧ or apply an erasure request⟦/f⟧,
    ⟦/f⟧⟦f:export-bundles⟧export, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:git-tracking⟧bind a repository identity by hand or rebind it, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:sandbox-risk⟧accept open
    residual risks (OWN-22), ⟦/f⟧⟦f:service-accounts⟧⟦f:principal-keys⟧certify a service account's principal key, ⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧assign a
    role, ⟦f:shared-rooms⟧set a room's admission, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:moderation⟧appoint a moderator⟦f:facilitator⟧ or the facilitator⟦/f⟧, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:stamps⟧stamp
    a pin version, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:ownership-transfer⟧name a successor, offer a handover, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:trust-grants⟧record a trust grant,
    ⟦/f⟧⟦f:notices⟧allow notices for a room or opt in to them, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:git-carrier⟧enable ⟦f:bridges⟧a bridge, which turns the
    bridge component on while any bridge stands enabled, or ⟦/f⟧the git carrier, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:moderation⟧set
    a room setting, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:publishing⟧⟦f:export-bundles⟧publish, ⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:purge-retention⟧⟦f:shared-rooms⟧apply a purge request, ⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:purge-retention⟧change a retention policy,
    ⟦/f⟧accept configuration (recording its digest), ⟦f:ci-attestation⟧enroll a CI key, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:principal-keys⟧rotate a
    device key, ⟦/f⟧⟦f:segment-exchange⟧retire a writer, ⟦/f⟧turn capture off or pause it⟦f:principal-keys⟧, enroll or revoke
    a device⟦f:peer-sync⟧, peer⟦/f⟧⟦f:presence-proof⟧ or authenticator⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:access-tokens⟧, mint or rotate an access token⟦/f⟧⟦f:witness-check⟧⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧, start a
    witness check, which confirms the command taken from an untrusted event
    (OWN-18)⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:store-protection⟧, and a backup restore⟦/f⟧.⟦f:principal-keys⟧ Revoking a device⟦f:peer-sync⟧ or a peer⟦/f⟧ stays widening
    although it undoes an enrollment, since it can drop pins and stop acts
    arriving.⟦/f⟧

  Any principal act that removes a pin from a restore block, or stops this node
  recording its own runs' events, is widening whatever verb carries it, so
  `parinn uninstall` records the widening act turning capture off before it
  removes the hook registrations (ADM-02). ⟦f:access-tokens⟧On an ephemeral node, PEER-01's
  environment variable, a structural event, stands in for turning on ⟦f:peer-sync⟧its peer
  component⟦f:git-carrier⟧ and⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:git-carrier⟧, for the git-carrier remotes its access token names, its publish
  component⟦/f⟧; minting that access token is the widening act. ⟦/f⟧⟦f:stamps⟧An unstamp⟦f:trust-grants⟧ and a
  trust-grant revocation⟦/f⟧ are the exceptions: each withdraws only the acting
  principal's own trust (LANE-32⟦f:trust-grants⟧, OWN-29⟦/f⟧). ⟦/f⟧⟦f:peer-sync⟧Applying a quarantine request takes
  the class of the quarantine it applies. ⟦/f⟧A principal act no requirement names
  is widening. Every principal act a requirement names is classed here, and
  OWN-11 follows.
⟦f:principal-keys⟧- **Expire act**: Once PRV-10 ships, an act a node with a device key records,
  signed with that key, ending only an expiry its original act set.⟦f:shared-rooms⟧ It ends a
  bar⟦f:moderation⟧, a mute⟦/f⟧⟦f:ownership-transfer⟧ or a handover offer⟦/f⟧ (LANE-25).⟦/f⟧⟦f:access-tokens⟧ It ends an access token, recorded
  by the node that minted it (PEER-05).⟦/f⟧⟦f:delegation-grants⟧ It ends a delegation grant⟦f:acceptance-grants⟧ or an
  acceptance grant⟦/f⟧, recorded by the node of the principal that recorded the
  grant (OWN-23⟦f:acceptance-grants⟧, OWN-26⟦/f⟧). Before PRV-10 ships no expiry can be set but a
  grant's, which then takes effect only as a refused delegation (Delegation
  grant).⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧
- **Role**: A named set of room capabilities: ⟦f:work-rooms⟧viewer, ⟦/f⟧contributor⟦f:moderation⟧ or moderator⟦/f⟧.
  The owner gives a seat its role by a **role assignment**. ⟦f:shared-rooms⟧⟦f:principal-keys⟧⟦f:work-rooms⟧An invite⟦f:access-tokens⟧ or invite
  link⟦/f⟧ records one for every seat that chains to the invited principal key and
  joins under it, run seats included⟦f:moderation⟧, though a run seat an invite names
  moderator is a contributor⟦/f⟧. ⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:paired-phone⟧A paired phone's personal-room seat has no role
  and reads within its device scope. ⟦/f⟧The seat ingest starts takes over the role
  of the run seat it names (REC-19). ⟦f:work-rooms⟧A seat with none, other than the owner's
  device seats, is a viewer; ⟦/f⟧a run's personal-room seat⟦f:work-rooms⟧, or its seat in a room
  it created,⟦/f⟧ is a contributor.⟦f:ownership-transfer⟧⟦f:moderation⟧ A handover records a moderator role assignment
  for the former owner's device seats (LANE-11).⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:moderation⟧ A run seat is a moderator only
  by appointment.⟦/f⟧⟦f:facilitator⟧⟦f:moderation⟧ Only the facilitator's device seat writes a room summary,
  beside its appointment.⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧
  ⟦f:work-rooms⟧- **Viewer:** read, a role request⟦f:facilitator⟧ and a summary request⟦/f⟧.⟦/f⟧
  - **Contributor:** read⟦f:facilitator⟧ and a summary request⟦/f⟧; ⟦f:conversation⟧post, ⟦/f⟧link⟦f:presentations⟧ and present⟦/f⟧; pin,
    edit and unpin its own pins, its **pin capability**, a device seat's own
    pins being every pin its principal wrote from a device seat⟦f:principal-keys⟧ within that
    seat's device scope⟦/f⟧; and work.
  ⟦f:moderation⟧- **Moderator:** a contributor's capabilities, plus a list removal of any pin⟦f:intent-criteria⟧
    but the intent⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧ or a verdict⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧, kick⟦f:shared-rooms⟧, bar, unbar⟦/f⟧, mute, unmute⟦f:presentations⟧, pick⟦/f⟧⟦f:work-rooms⟧, and set
    title, labels and assignments⟦/f⟧.⟦/f⟧
- **Capability**: What a role lets a seat do. The closed set LANE-16 lists: what
  the ⟦f:moderation⟧three ⟦/f⟧roles list⟦f:facilitator⟧⟦f:moderation⟧, plus writing a room summary, which only the
  facilitator's appointment carries⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧.
- **Work**: A capability, not an act: to edit, execute commands⟦f:git-tracking⟧, write worktree
  checkpoints and commit⟦/f⟧ (LANE-16); a run's events go to its run seat as
  Relations says⟦f:work-rooms⟧; an assignment only asks⟦/f⟧. As a capability, "work" means nothing
  else; what one agent hands another is a delegated task.
⟦f:moderation⟧- **Appointment**: A principal act that makes a run seat⟦f:shared-rooms⟧, or a device seat of a
  principal other than the owner,⟦/f⟧ an **appointed moderator**, a moderator within
  SEC-32's limits. The owner may appoint⟦f:shared-rooms⟧, and so may a principal whose device
  seat has the moderator role by role assignment⟦f:facilitator⟧, except the facilitator, whom
  only the owner appoints⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧. The appointer or the owner may revoke it.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:work-rooms⟧- **Join**: The act that adds a seat to a room⟦f:shared-rooms⟧ under its admission, or without
  it for a device seat whose principal has a member seat there⟦/f⟧. A run joins only
  when its principal asks for the join or accepts it (LANE-23). ⟦f:git-tracking⟧That covers the
  branches the room names later by branch links, whose runs' events then go
  there (LANE-01), so a branch link stays a room act. ⟦/f⟧A device seat joins by a
  join room act its principal takes at a principal surface. Its node also joins
  it before recording there a principal⟦f:principal-keys⟧ or expire⟦/f⟧ act⟦f:purge-retention⟧, a tombstone⟦f:peer-sync⟧, an erasure
  request a retention policy sends⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:launcher⟧⟦f:git-tracking⟧, or ⟦f:bridges⟧a bridge's or ⟦/f⟧the launcher's event about
  a room's branch⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:shared-rooms⟧, without admission when its principal has a member seat there⟦/f⟧.
  ⟦f:paired-phone⟧A paired phone never joins. ⟦/f⟧An owner whose seats have all left rejoins⟦f:shared-rooms⟧⟦f:principal-keys⟧ under
  admission, which its principal key always satisfies (Admission)⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧. **Leave** is
  a seat's room act ending its own add.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:moderation⟧- **Kick**: Revokes a seat's current add. Only that seat's principal may add it
  again (LANE-25).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:shared-rooms⟧- **Bar**: ⟦f:principal-keys⟧Names a principal key and keeps every key that chains to it out,
  until an unbar or an expire act (LANE-25).⟦/f⟧ Its setter⟦f:moderation⟧ where SEC-32
  permits, the setter's appointer⟦/f⟧ or the owner may unbar.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:moderation⟧- **Mute**: Withdraws every capability but read from one seat or from the whole
  room⟦f:conversation⟧; a whole-room mute leaves posting to the roles the owner names⟦/f⟧ (LANE-16).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:presentations⟧- **Present**: Puts a presentation in the outcome window.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:presentations⟧- **Pick**: Chooses which presentation the outcome window shows.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:shared-rooms⟧- **Admission**: ⟦f:principal-keys⟧Whether a room is invite only or admits a list of principal
  keys. An invite (a principal key and a role)⟦f:access-tokens⟧ and an invite link⟦/f⟧ are widening
  principal acts of the owner. The owner's principal key always satisfies its
  room's admission, for its device and run seats alike. ⟦/f⟧An invite's⟦f:export-bundles⟧, an export's⟦/f⟧
  ⟦f:publishing⟧⟦f:export-bundles⟧or a publish's ⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧**review step** shows the acting principal, before it takes
  effect, what will take effect or leave, SEC-08 applied (LANE-10⟦f:export-bundles⟧, SEC-26⟦/f⟧).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:ownership-transfer⟧- **Successor**: A principal the owner names in advance, who accepts ownership
  once every seat of the owner has left the room; that acceptance is a
  **succession**. Until a handover, a succession or the owner's rejoin, a room
  whose owner left keeps its pins as they were⟦f:stamps⟧, but a stamper may still unstamp⟦/f⟧
  (LANE-11⟦f:stamps⟧, LANE-32⟦/f⟧).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:ownership-transfer⟧- **Handover**: Transfers ownership by an offer and an acceptance. Succession is
  the other path to ownership.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:stamps⟧- **Stamp**: The act of a principal with a seat in the room on one pin version,
  after being shown its exact text, author and key fingerprint. A stamped
  version of a type that restores restores word for word to that principal's own
  agents only. An edit, an unpin⟦f:moderation⟧ or a list removal⟦/f⟧ leaves a stamped version
  restoring until its stamper unstamps it, a cut principal act (LANE-32).⟦/f⟧
- **Active pin**: A pin on its room's pin list (I10).
- **Room merge**: The one rule deriving all room state from the ⟦f:principal-keys⟧three ⟦/f⟧act kinds,
  in causal order (LANE-31). Seats that are members with no add, and the seat
  ingest starts, stand beside it. It covers membership, roles, ⟦f:moderation⟧appointments,
  ⟦/f⟧pins, pin versions⟦f:stamps⟧, stamps⟦/f⟧⟦f:moderation⟧, mutes⟦/f⟧⟦f:presentations⟧, presentations, picks⟦/f⟧⟦f:shared-rooms⟧, bars⟦/f⟧⟦f:ownership-transfer⟧, handovers and
  their offers⟦/f⟧⟦f:room-status⟧, OWN-21's ready and abandoned marks⟦/f⟧⟦f:ci-attestation⟧, the CI keys enrolled in the
  room⟦/f⟧⟦f:git-carrier⟧ and whether the git carrier is enabled for it⟦/f⟧.⟦f:work-rooms⟧ It covers ⟦f:ownership-transfer⟧the successor,
  ⟦/f⟧title, labels, assignment, visibility⟦f:shared-rooms⟧, admission⟦/f⟧⟦f:notices⟧, the notice allowance⟦/f⟧⟦f:moderation⟧ and the
  **room settings** (⟦f:conversation⟧whether drafts show live, whether typing shows, the roles a
  whole-room mute leaves posting to, and ⟦/f⟧the **appointment rate**: how many
  kicks⟦f:shared-rooms⟧, bars⟦/f⟧ and mutes an appointed moderator may set per period⟦f:conversation⟧, PEER-09⟦/f⟧,
  SEC-32)⟦/f⟧.⟦/f⟧ When acts conflict, the more restrictive act wins, then the lower
  commitment. ⟦f:presentations⟧Concurrent picks resolve by **pick order** (⟦f:facilitator⟧the facilitator's
  seat, then ⟦/f⟧⟦f:moderation⟧any other moderator, then ⟦/f⟧the owner, VIEW-22). ⟦/f⟧⟦f:work-rooms⟧⟦f:git-tracking⟧Of two branch links
  naming one branch, the first in causal order stands, concurrent ones by the
  lower commitment (LANE-01). ⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧Acts with no member seat: open (OQ-41).
- **Concurrent**: Of two acts or events: neither causally after the other;
  **causal order** puts each after every act or event it saw.
- **Room state**: Everything the room merge derives (LANE-31).
